<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Results</h2>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Identifiability)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An encoder <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\rightarrow Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\rightarrow Z</annotation></semantics></math> identifies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists a permutation <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and functions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}:\mathcal{S}_{i}\rightarrow Z_{\pi(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}:\mathcal{S}_{i}\rightarrow Z_{\pi(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> that are diffeomorphism such that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}=h(z_{\pi(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}=h(z_{\pi(i)})</annotation></semantics></math>.
That is, each latent factor learned is equivalent to a ground truth factor up to a permutation.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Local</span> Identifiability of the Independently Controllable Factors)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the learned encoder <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\rightarrow Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\rightarrow Z</annotation></semantics></math> be a diffeomorphism.
If the following conditions hold</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The action effects are </span><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">sufficiently different</span><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> from the natural dynamics. That is, there exists </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[K]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial s_{i}^{\prime}}\frac{T_{i}(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a)}{T(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}\neq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial s_{i}^{\prime}}\frac{T_{i}(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a)}{T(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\tilde{S}\subseteq\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\tilde{S}\subseteq\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, almost surely. Moreover, there exists at least an action that affects each </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (independently controllability)</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All energy function approximate the factor forward dynamics </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(z_{i}^{\prime},a,z)\propto\log T(z_{i}^{\prime}\mid z,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(z_{i}^{\prime},a,z)\propto\log T(z_{i}^{\prime}\mid z,a)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Sparsity</span><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) The learned score differences</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{i}^{\prime}}\Delta E_{i}^{a}=\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{i}^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{i}^{\prime},a,z)-E(z_{i}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right]\neq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>a</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{i}^{\prime}}\Delta E_{i}^{a}=\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{i}^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{i}^{\prime},a,z)-E(z_{i}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right]\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for at most one variable </span><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then, there exists a factor-wise diffeomorphism <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow Z</annotation></semantics></math> between the learned encoding <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> and the underlying ground truth factors of variation <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> be a diffeomorphism between <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given that the ground truth observation function is a diffeomorphism <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow X</annotation></semantics></math> and, by assumption, the learned encoding is also a diffeomorphism. We can see that <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(s)=f(o(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(s)=f(o(s))</annotation></semantics></math>.
We need to prove that there exists a permutation <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:[K]\rightarrow[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:[K]\rightarrow[K]</annotation></semantics></math> such that the permuted Jacobian of <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi}J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi}J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a diagonal matrix.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given that <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is a diffeomorphism, <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> exists.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, for each binary classifier, we know that at an optimum they converge to:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}=\sum_{l=1}^{K}E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)+C(z,a_{n})\;\;\forall a_{n}\in A\setminus\{a_{0}\};" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.727em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}=\sum_{l=1}^{K}E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)+C(z,a_{n})\;\;\forall a_{n}\in A\setminus\{a_{0}\};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(z,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(z,a)</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant resulting from the normalization constants that are not estimated in ACF.
By taking the gradient with respect to <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> using the chain rule, we get that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{s^{\prime}}\log\frac{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}=\sum_{l=1}^{K}J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\nabla_{z^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right]\;\;\forall a_{n}\in A\setminus\{a_{0}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.727em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{s^{\prime}}\log\frac{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}=\sum_{l=1}^{K}J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\nabla_{z^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right]\;\;\forall a_{n}\in A\setminus\{a_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(a_{i})\mapsto[K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(a_{i})\mapsto[K]</annotation></semantics></math> be the maps each action to its affected factor. Hence, by considering our sparse interaction model in Equation <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Problem Formulation ‣ 3 ACF: Action Controllable Factorization ‣ From Pixels to Factors:Learning Independently Controllable State Variables for Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we get that each classifier is a function of the variables affected by <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
That is,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{s^{\prime}}\log\frac{T(s_{\rho(a_{n})}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s_{\rho(a_{n})}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{s^{\prime}}\log\frac{T(s_{\rho(a_{n})}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s_{\rho(a_{n})}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{l=1}^{K}J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\nabla_{z^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right]\;\;\forall a_{n}\in A\setminus\{a_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.727em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{l=1}^{K}J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\nabla_{z^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right]\;\;\forall a_{n}\in A\setminus\{a_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J_{h}^{T}\left[\begin{matrix}\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{1}^{\prime}}(E(z_{1}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{1}^{\prime},a_{0},z))\\
\vdots\\
\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{K}^{\prime}}(E(z_{K}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{K}^{\prime},a_{0},z))\end{matrix}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J_{h}^{T}\left[\begin{matrix}\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{1}^{\prime}}(E(z_{1}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{1}^{\prime},a_{0},z))\\
\vdots\\
\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{K}^{\prime}}(E(z_{K}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{K}^{\prime},a_{0},z))\end{matrix}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, consider a set of the actions <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathcal{A}}\subseteq\mathcal{A}\setminus\{a_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathcal{A}}\subseteq\mathcal{A}\setminus\{a_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that each action affects one of the ground truth variables, that is, they are independently controllable.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can write the above conditions in matrix form by stacking the gradients of all the actions in <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)</annotation></semantics></math> be the matrices of learned score differences</span></p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)]_{l,n}=\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{l}^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right];" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)]_{l,n}=\frac{\partial}{\partial z_{l}^{\prime}}\left[E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{n},z)-E(z_{l}^{\prime},a_{0},z)\right];</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> be the matrices of score differences in <math id="A1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)]_{i,n}=\begin{cases}\frac{\partial}{\partial{s_{i}^{\prime}}}\log\frac{T(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}&amp;\text{if }i=\rho(a_{n})\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)]_{i,n}=\begin{cases}\frac{\partial}{\partial{s_{i}^{\prime}}}\log\frac{T(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{n})}{T(s_{i}^{\prime}\mid s,a_{0})}&amp;\text{if }i=\rho(a_{n})\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we can rewrite Equation <a href="#A1.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Results ‣ From Pixels to Factors:Learning Independently Controllable State Variables for Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)=J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)=J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">There exists <math id="A1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> such that all columns of <math id="A1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> has only one element different from zero and it is full rank because each factor is affected by at least one action.
Moreover, given <math id="A1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is full rank because is a diffeomorphism and <math id="A1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)</annotation></semantics></math> must also have exactly one element different from zero (sparsity condition).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, <math id="A1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> must have only one element different from zero per row.
To see this, consider the <math id="A1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th column of <math id="A1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)_{j}=\beta e_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)_{j}=\beta e_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the row different from zero. Hence,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta S(s^{\prime}\mid s)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)_{j};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})\Delta S(z^{\prime}\mid z)_{j};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})e_{r};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})e_{r};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})_{:,r};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta J_{h}^{T}(s^{\prime})_{:,r};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">and, therefore, <math id="A1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(s^{\prime})_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(s^{\prime})_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> the <math id="A1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>th column of the Jacobian must have one element different from zero. Therefore, <math id="A1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> must be <math id="A1.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-sparse.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, there exists a permutation <math id="A1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(s^{\prime})=P(s^{\prime})D(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(s^{\prime})=P(s^{\prime})D(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix. That is, there exists <math id="A1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> that is a factorwise transformation of <math id="A1.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> up to a permutation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">This lemma shows that the there exists a permutation in <math id="A1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> where action can have independent control over the factors. However, this does not guarantee the encoding is consistent because the permutation could be different in other parts of the space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">The following proposition establishes some conditions that guarantee identifiability globally.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Global Identifiability of Independently Controllable Factors)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the local conditions for identifiability hold. Moreover, assume that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subset\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subset\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is connected. Then there exists a unique permutation <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be a fix point.
We know that the Jacobian <math id="A1.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(s_{0})=P_{\pi}(s_{0})D(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(s_{0})=P_{\pi}(s_{0})D(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> because of local identifiability. Let <math id="A1.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{s_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{s_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the permutation corresponding to the matrix <math id="A1.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi}(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi}(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, because <math id="A1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is a diffeomorphism, we have that each derivative <math id="A1.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}^{\prime}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}^{\prime}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and non-vanishing.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, there exists a neighborhood <math id="A1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\pi_{s_{0}}(i)}(s_{\pi_{s_{0}}(i)})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\pi_{s_{0}}(i)}(s_{\pi_{s_{0}}(i)})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because of continuity of <math id="A1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have that per each row it’s nonzero element remains so and, similarly, for the zero elements of the row.
Therefore, the permutation <math id="A1.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{s_{0}}=\pi_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{s_{0}}=\pi_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in U</annotation></semantics></math>. This makes the permutation locally constant.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, because there’s a finite discrete number of permutations and <math id="A1.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is connected, it implies that <math id="A1.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{s}=\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{s}=\pi</annotation></semantics></math> globally constant in <math id="A1.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Extended Empirical Results</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Anonymized code at <a href="https://anonymous.4open.science/r/factored_rl-EE0A" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://anonymous.4open.science/r/factored_rl-EE0A</a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Network Architectures</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All networks were implemented using JAX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bradbury et al., 2018</a>)</cite> and Flax NNX <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Heek et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>All methods use the same Residual Convolutional architecture for encoder (and decoder, when required). All MLPs use SiLU activations. Latent encodings are Tanh to keep between <math id="A2.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> except for DMS.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T2.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T2.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Component</span></th>
<td id="A2.T2.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">DoorKey(8x8)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Taxi</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Grid2D</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T2.6.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">FourRooms</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.6.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">latent_dim <math id="A2.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d)</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<td id="A2.T2.6.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T2.6.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">7</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T2.6.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">6</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T2.6.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">2</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T2.6.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.6.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.6.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A2.T2.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">n_actions <math id="A2.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<td id="A2.T2.6.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T2.6.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">10</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T2.6.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">6</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T2.6.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5</span></td>
<td id="A2.T2.6.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T2.6.3.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">10</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T2.6.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T2.6.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.T2.6.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">ACF Energy[<math id="A2.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times d</annotation></semantics></math>]</span></th>
<td id="A2.T2.6.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" colspan="4"><math id="A2.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d+n_{a})\to 256\to n_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">256</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">n</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d+n_{a})\to 256\to n_{a}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
